hadiths[269]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2453","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the months of Hajj are Shawwal, Dhul-Qa'd and Dhul-Hijj."
"2454","Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Zubair (RA) narrates that the month of Hajj is Shawwal, Dhu al-Qa’da and the first ten days of Dhu Hajj."
"2455","Abu Shaykh narrates: I asked Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) about the months of Hajj, and he replied that Shawwal is the ten days of Dhul-Qa'dah and Dhul-Hijj."
"2456","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says, \The months of Hajj are fixed.\"" Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) says that this Shawwal is the ten days of Dhul-Qa'dah and Dhul-Hijj."""""
"2457","The same hadith has been narrated along with another chain of transmission on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"2458","The same hadith has been narrated along with another chain of transmission on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"2459","Abdul Aziz bin Rabi narrates this from his grandfather on the authority of his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave a sermon in the middle of the days of Tashriq (the narrator narrates), this means on the day of the first departure."
"2460","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates about the saying of Allah (Glory be to the Almighty) “So whoever makes Hajj obligatory among them” Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) says, what this means is that he should make the intention of Ihram."
"2461","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zubair (RA) says that making Hajj obligatory means putting on Ihram."
"2462","Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that making Hajj obligatory means putting on Ihram (i.e. intending to do it)."
"2463","Sayyiduna Udi bin Hatim (RA) narrates, “I attended the service of the Holy Prophet (PBUH) and the Prophet (PBUH) said to me, “Soon a woman will depart from Hira until she circumambulates this house and she will fear only Allah (there will be no fear of anyone else besides Him).”"
"2464","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says: I heard the Prophet (PBUH) while giving a sermon in Arafat saying, \Whoever does not have shoes should wear socks and whoever does not have an apron should wear trousers.\"""""""
"2465","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"2466","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this about Muharram. \When he does not have shoes"","" he should wear socks and when he does not have an apron"","" he should wear shalwar.\"""""""
"2467","Sayyidna Jabir (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said, \He who does not have shoes should wear socks"","" and if he does not have an apron"","" he should wear shalwar.\"""""""
"2468","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that a person who cannot find shoes should wear socks and a person who cannot find an apron should wear shalwar."
"2469","Sayyidna Jabir (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this: \He who does not find shoes should wear socks"","" but cut them below the ankles.\"" A narrator named Abbas narrates that if Muharram does not find shoes"","" he should wear socks"","" but he should cut them both in such a way that they reach below both ankles."""""
"2470","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying while delivering a sermon, \Whoever does not have shoes should wear socks and whoever does not have an apron should wear pants.\"""""""
"2471","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said this: \Whoever does not have an apron should wear shalwar"","" and whoever does not have shoes"","" should wear socks.\"" (Imam Darqutni"","" may God have mercy on him) narrates that this refers to Madinah before wearing Ihram. While other narrators have narrated the hadith regarding Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas"","" it mentions that"","" Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" heard the Prophet saying that while giving a sermon"","" so this hadith will be after the hadith narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar"","" may Allah be pleased with him."""""
"2472","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (SAW) \Whoever does not get shoes"","" he should wear socks"","" but he should cut them from the bottom up to the ankles.\"""""""
"2473","Salim narrates this statement of his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him): A person asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, what clothes should a person in the state of Ihram wear? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He will not wear a shirt, he will not wear a turban, he will not wear shalwar, he will not wear a hat, and he will not wear a cloth that has varus or saffron on it, he will not wear socks. A narrator named Yusuf has quoted these words: \Cut the ants so that they reach below the ankles.\"""""""
"2474","Safwan bin Ya'ila narrates this statement of his father: I wanted to see the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in such a state that he was receiving revelation. Once when we were in Jarana and the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was also there. A person came who was wearing a Jabba and tied the Ihram of Umrah and he also applied perfume. He said, O Messenger of Allah! You say about such a person who has made the intention of Haram in his life. At the same time, the revelation began to be revealed to the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he started snoring. After that, this state of his ended. So you inquired where is the person who had just asked me a question? This person was brought. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “As for the modesty, take it off, and as for the fragrance, wash it and put on Ihram again.” Abu Abd al-Rahman (Imam al-Nasa'i, may God have mercy on him) narrated this. To the best of my knowledge, no one has narrated this saying, 'The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed this person to put on Ihram again."
"2475","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said, \A person in the state of Ihram can kill rats"","" scorpions"","" mad dogs"","" and crows.\"""""""
"2476","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that a person in the state of Ihram can kill a wolf, a crow, an eagle, and a mouse."
"2477","This same hadith along with another chain of transmission has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar."
"2478","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade wearing a shirt and wearing socks (in the state of Ihram)."
"2479","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this on the authority of Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) who said that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to smell the best perfume while putting on Ihram."
"2480","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that a person in the state of Ihram can smell a basil (scented) flower, he can enter the bath, he can pull out a tooth, he can tear open an abscess, and when his nail breaks, he can remove the pain from you."
"2481","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that there is no harm in using a belt and a ring for a person in the state of Ihram."
"2482","It has been narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) that a person in the state of Ihram is allowed to wear a ring and tie a waist belt."
"2483","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) states that there is no problem in wearing a ring for a person in the state of Ihram."
"2484","This same hadith is transmitted along with another chain of transmission, however, it does not mention that it was transmitted from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas."
"2485","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that when we used to travel with the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he used to say Takbeer when he walked on high ground, and when he descended to low ground, he used to say Subhan Allah."
"2486","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates this, and the Sunnah of Hajj includes this: \A man who performs Hajj in the month of Ihram has been followed by some other narrators.\"" His narrator is Abul Qasim"","" who is the imam of Abdullah bin Harith's Azad."""""
"2487","It is narrated that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said this about a person who puts on the Ihram for Hajj before the months of Hajj. He said that this is not a Sunnah."
"2488","Abu Zubayr narrates: I asked Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) whether it is permissible to wear Ihram before the beginning of the month of Hajj. He answered no!"
"2489","Ata narrates that Allah Ta'ala has said this: \The months of Hajj are fixed\"" and the reason for this is that a person should not wear the Ihram of Hajj before that."""""
"2490","Salim narrates about Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that he used to refuse to set conditions for Hajj and said, \Isn't the Sunnah of your Prophet sufficient for you?\"""""""
"2491","The same hadith has been narrated along with another chain of transmission. However, it contains these words (he said) The Sunnah of your Prophet is sufficient. He did not set any conditions."
"2492","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) went to Sayyida Zaba’ah Bint Zubair (RA) and said, “O Messenger of Allah! I intend to perform Hajj, but I am sick. The Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said, \Make up your mind and make a condition that I will open Ihram where I am not able to go further.\"""""""
"2493","Sayyidna Abdullah Bin Abbas Radiyallahu Anhuma Sayyidah Dabba'ah Bint Zubayr Radiyallahu Anhu came to the service of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \Put on Ihram and make it a condition that I will open Ihram where I am not able to go further.\"" The narrator says that he had performed Hajj."""""
"2494","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"2495","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"2496","Sayyid Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed the Zubayah (to wear Ihram)."
"2497","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appointed Zaat-e-Irq as a miqat for the people of Iraq."
"2498","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"2499","Amro bin Shuaib narrates on the authority of his father and grandfather that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appointed Zaat-i-Irq as the Miqat for the people of Iraq."
"2500","The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission in which these words are said: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) (after that he mentioned the entire hadith and said: It is) appointed Zaat-e-Irq as Miqat for the people of Iraq."
"2501","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet appointed Dhul-Halifa for the people of Madinah, Yallam for the people of Yemen, Hajfah for the people of Egypt, and Zaat-Irq for the people of Iraq."
"2502","Sayyiduna Harith bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that I attended the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he was in Mina at that time (after that he mentioned the entire hadith in which he stated that) he appointed Yallam as a miqat for the people of Yemen, that they would put on Ihram from there, and Zaat-Irq (assigned a miqat) for the people of Iraq."
"2503","Abu Zubair narrates: He heard Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) and inquired from him about putting on Ihram, and he narrated this with reference to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: The place for the people of Madinah to put on Ihram is Dhul-Halifa, while the other way is Hajfah."
"2504","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, it has been narrated as a hadith that the Prophet appointed Dhu’l-Halifa for the people of Medina, Hajfah for the people of Syria, Qarn for the people of Najd (the word Qarn Al-Mazil) for the people of Yemen, and Yalmalum for the people of Yemen. (There are these words in one tradition) He will put on Ihram from his house, (And in one tradition there are these words) He will put on Ihram from wherever he wants. Even the people of Makkah will put on Ihram in Makkah."
"2505","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"2506","Khalid Ibn Sa'ib narrates this statement of his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gabriel came to me and he said to me: I should instruct my companions to recite Talbiyyah in a loud voice."
"2507","Amara bin Khuzamah narrates this statement of his father: When the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished reciting Talbiyah, he prayed to Allah for His forgiveness and approval and sought refuge in His mercy from Hell."
"2508","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) performed Hajj."
"2509","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that we had put on Ihram for the Hajj people with the Prophet (PBUH)."
"2510","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) first appointed Sayyidna Uttab bin Usayd (may God be pleased with him) as Ameer al-Hajj, so he performed the Hajj, then in 9 Hijra he appointed Sayyidna Abu Bakr (may God be pleased with him) as Ameer al-Hajj, and he also performed the Hajj in 10 Hijri. Then Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) also performed Hajj in person, then he also performed Hajj in person, then Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may God be pleased with him) passed away, then Sayyiduna Umar (may God be pleased with him) became the caliph. Umar (RA) passed away and Sayyidna Uthman (RA) became the caliph, so he also performed Hajj."
"2511","Abd al-Rahman bin Aswad narrates this statement of his father: I performed Hajj with Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (RA) He performed Hajj I performed Hajj with Sayyidna Umar (RA) He performed Hajj I performed Hajj with Sayyidna Uthman (RA) He performed Hajj."
"2512","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) used to make his back in a state of haraam."
"2513","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) was walking between Makkah and Madinah (i.e. during the journey) 'The Prophet (PBUH) was both fasting and in the state of Ihram at that time."
"2514","Narrated by Sayyidna Urwah bin Mudhars (RA) I came to the service of the Holy Prophet (PBUH) and asked him what had happened while he was staying in Muzdalifah. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah! I am present at your service from the two mountains of Behar. I have tired my rider and I have also tired myself. By Allah! I have camped near every mountain, then my Hajj will be done, O Messenger of Allah! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Whoever performed the morning prayer with us in Muzdalifah and who reached Arafat before that at night or during the day, he has fulfilled his vow and his Hajj is complete."
"2515","Sayyidna Urwa bin Mudras (RA) narrates, “I attended the service of the Holy Prophet (PBUH) and he was in Muzdalifah at that time.” I said, “O Messenger of Allah! Did I have Hajj? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Whoever performs this prayer with us and stays with us until we leave, or whoever leaves Arafat at night or before it during the day, his Hajj will be completed and he has fulfilled his vow."
"2516","Sayyidna Abd al-Rahman bin Yamar Deli narrates: I attended the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He was encamped in Arafa at that time. What is Hajj? The Holy Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Hajj Arafa (the name of the person standing) is one who reaches Arafa before dawn on the day of sacrifice."
"2517","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"2518","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) said, “Whoever stands at Arafat during the night, he has performed Hajj, and whoever does not stand at Arafat during the night, his Hajj will be completed, so he wears Ihram for Umrah, and it will be necessary for him to perform Hajj the next year.” The narrator named Rahmat bin Musab is weak."
"2519","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, has said that whoever reaches Arafat and stops there and also reaches Muzdalifah, his Hajj will be completed, and whoever cannot reach Arafat, he cannot perform Hajj, he should put on Ihram for Umrah."
"2520","Ibrahim Taymi quotes this statement of Sayyiduna Abu Zarghafari (RA) regarding his father. By Allah! The order of Hajj Tamattu was reserved only for us or for the person who was besieged."
"2521","Harith bin Bilal narrates this statement of his father: I said, O Messenger of Allah! The order to cancel Hajj is only for us or for those after us? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No! It is only for us."
"2522","Ibrahim Taymi narrates that his father narrated this about Sayyiduna Abu'd Radiyallahu Anhu. It is reserved only for us i.e. the Companions of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). It is not for the rest of the people."
"2523","Sayyiduna Abu Zarghafari (RA) says that no one has the right to enjoy Hajj, he should only put on Ihram for Hajj and cancel it again through Umrah, except for those riders who were with the Prophet (PBUH)."
"2524","Sayyiduna Abu Zar Ghaffari (RA) says that no one has the right to do this after us. He should first put on Ihram for Hajj and then cancel it and change it to Umrah before performing Hajj."
"2525","Sayyiduna Abu Zarghafari (RA) says that no one has the right to cancel Hajj by performing Umrah after putting on Ihram."
"2526","Qasim bin Muhammad narrates about Sayyida Aisha, she came (for Hajj) with two sacrificial animals. Both of them were lost, so Sayyidna Abdullah bin Zubair, may Allah be pleased with them, sent two more animals to the service of Sayyida Aisha. He slaughtered them and said that this is the Sunnah about sacrificial animals."
"2527","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates, “I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying: “Whoever takes a sacrificial animal and then loses it, it is not obligatory on him to replace it."
"2528","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who sent a sacrificial animal and then that animal (lost or died), then if that person wants, he can replace it with another animal."
"2529","Both Sayyidna Masurab bin Mukharama (RA) and Marwan Bin Huqm (R.A.) narrated that the Prophet (PBUH) sacrificed seventy camels on behalf of seven hundred men at Hudaybiyyah."
"2530","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that on the occasion of Eid al-Adha, one camel will be sacrificed by ten men."
"2531","This tradition is also narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, one of its narrators is Ayyub Abu Jamal Zaeef and only he has narrated this tradition regarding Ata."
"2532","Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) has prescribed this Sunnah: Cows and camels will be sacrificed by seven men."
"2533","Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) narrates that we sacrificed seventy camels on the occasion of the Peace of Hudaybiyyah. One camel belonged to seven men. On that day, the Prophet (PBUH) said that a few people should sacrifice one animal together."
"2534","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that whoever forgets or abandons any of the rituals of Hajj, he will have to make a sacrifice."
"2535","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"2536","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that if a person abandons any of his rituals, he will make a sacrifice."
"2537","Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this statement of Sayyidna Ka'b bin Asim Ash'ari (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave a sermon in the mud on the middle of Eid al-Adha (says the narrator), that is, the day after the sacrifice."
"2538","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that expiation is given on purpose."
"2539","Sayyiduna Jabar bin Abdullah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"2540","Abd al-Rahman bin Abu Ammar narrates: We asked Sayyiduna Jabar bin Abdullah (RA) about the cave, and he said, \It is necessary to make a hole in it.\"" I asked"","" \""Is this necessary?\"" He replied yes"","" he said that it is necessary."""""
"2541","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “The wound is a victim (says the narrator) and the Holy Prophet (may Allah bless him and grant him peace) has prescribed the payment of expiation for the scaly in it."
"2542","Abd al-Rahman bin Abu Ammar narrates this about Sayyiduna Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him: He says, \I found out that it is possible to eat the goh?\"" He answered yes! I wonder if it is hunting? He answered yes! I inquired"","" have you heard this from the mouth of the Holy Prophet (peace be upon him)? He replied yes!"""""
"2543","Ibn Abu Ammar narrates: I asked Sayyiduna Jabar bin Abdullah (RA) about the cave. He answered yes! I asked: Can it be eaten? He said yes! I inquired, have you heard this from the mouth of the Holy Prophet (peace be upon him)? He replied yes!"
"2544","Abd al-Rahman bin Abu Ammar narrates that he inquired from Sayyiduna Jabir (may God be pleased with him) about Goh. He inquired whether it can be eaten. Sayyiduna Jabir answered yes! I wonder if it is hunting? You answered yes! I inquired, have you heard this from the mouth of the Holy Prophet (peace be upon him)? He replied yes!"
"2545","Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) was asked about the cave, and the Prophet (PBUH) said, \It is hunting.\"" (The narrator says) If a person in the state of Ihram kills him"","" then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has prescribed the sacrifice of a drumstick."""""
"2546","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “If a person in the state of Ihram kills it, he must pay for it, and about the deer, he said: “A goat must be sacrificed. It is an animal that walks."
"2547","It has been narrated about Sayyidna Jabir (R.A.) that he had given a decision to sacrifice a bullock in the hunting of a cave."
"2548","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated this ruling regarding the pigeon of the sanctuary: \The expiation for killing a pigeon in the sanctuary will be a goat; the expiation for damaging an egg will be one dirham; for killing an ostrich"","" a camel must be sacrificed; for killing a cow"","" a cow must be sacrificed; and for killing a cow"","" a cow must be sacrificed.\"""""""
"2549","Sayyidna Jabir (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) had given this decision about the deer: 'A goat must be sacrificed'. He said that the child who has been weaned and can walk."
"2550","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates this statement of Sayyidna Ka'b bin Ajrah (RA) that the Prophet (PBUH) gave this decision regarding an ostrich egg: \If a person in the state of Ihram harms it"","" he must pay a ransom according to its value.\"""""""
"2551","This tradition is narrated along with another document, but there is some wording difference in it."
"2552","Muawiya bin Qura narrated this from an Ansari elder: A man was riding his horse in the state of Ihram, he came to an ostrich's nest and picked up an egg that fell from his hand, then Sayyiduna Ali bin Abu Talib (R.A.) decreed about him that he would buy the daughters of Mukhaz, give them to Jafti, then the children she would give birth to would be donated to the House of Allah, and Even if these camels did not give birth to a child, the expiation of that person will be paid, because sometimes a child comes out of an egg and sometimes a child does not come out. Yes, the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, in exchange for each egg, one should feed a poor person or fast for one day (expiation)."
"2553","This tradition is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyidna Ali bin Abu Talib (RA)."
"2554","This tradition is narrated from an Ansari companion along with another chain of transmission."
"2555","Abd al-Rahman bin Abu Laila narrated this about Sayyidna Ali, may Allah be pleased with him: Once a man put an ostrich's nest under the feet of his camel. He came to the service of the Prophet and mentioned this to the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him. Then the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said, Ali has said what he had to say about this, but why do you not come to leave? You will be required to fast one day or eat one day for each one."
"2556","Mu'awiya bin Qura narrated that a man built an ostrich's nest under the feet of his camel. He asked Sayyidna Ali (RA) about it. Sayyidna Ali (RA) said, \In exchange for each egg"","" you have to give one camel as a mate or pay for the baby in the camel's belly.\"" Anhu said to him: Yes. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have heard what he said. Why don't you come to leave? For one egg you have to fast for a day and feed a poor person."""""
"2557","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that in exchange for an ostrich egg, one should fast for one day or feed a poor person."
"2558","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"2559","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave this decision about an egg which was broken by a man in the state of Ihram (the decision of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was that one day of fasting should be observed in exchange for one egg)."
"2560","It was narrated from Umm al-Mu'minin Sayyidah Aisha that the Messenger of Allah, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: In the ransom of this egg of the camel; A narrator named Abu Khalid narrates that if a person in the state of Ihram breaks an ostrich egg, he will fast for one day."
"2561","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave this decision regarding an ostrich egg (this egg was broken by a person in the state of Ihram, that person will fast for one egg)."
"2562","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this about the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). It has been said about the egg, if a person in the state of Ihram breaks it, he will pay for it."
"2563","It has been narrated about Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, that once some people killed a caveman and Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, said that all these people will be required to sacrifice one piece of meat, which they will perform together."
"2564","Narrator of Amarnami states that some slaves of Ibn Zubair were in the state of Ihram. \Once a woman passed by them. They killed her with sticks. Then they were confused about this. They came to the service of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) and mentioned this to him. Sayyidna Abdullah Bin Umar (RA) said: \""You will be required to sacrifice a stick.\"" Will it be necessary? So Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said"","" \""You are doing too much for yourselves. You will all have to sacrifice one piece of meat.\"" The lexicographers said: These words of the hadith are meant by lamazirbakum"","" in this case you will abuse yourself."""""
"2565","Sayyiduna Usama bin Sharik (RA) narrates, “I went to perform Hajj with the Holy Prophet (PBUH)” People came to serve him “Someone was saying this, O Messenger of Allah! I have tried before performing Tawaf, or I have postponed a thing, or I have taken one of the members first, then this is what the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was saying, there is no harm, except for the person who harms the honor of a Muslim and he is a transgressor, this person will suffer embarrassment and will be killed."
"2566","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (RA) narrates that a person asked the Prophet (PBUH) and said, “I have performed ablution before performing the sacrifice! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \You take the sacrifice now. There is no problem. Another person said: I have done the sacrifice before hitting the pebbles!\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said"","" \""You now throw pebbles!\"" There is no problem."""""
"2567","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amro bin Al-Aas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that on the day of sacrifice, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stopped on his horse. People started asking him questions. One of them said, O Messenger of Allah! I didn't know that 'pebbles must be thrown before the sacrifice'. I have already sacrificed before throwing the pebbles. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \Now throw the pebbles"","" there is no harm.\"" The other person said"","" O Messenger of Allah! I did not know that the sacrifice will be done before shaving the head. It was done before. The Holy Prophet (peace be upon him) said to him"","" \""Do it now. There is no problem.\"""""""
"2568","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"2569","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (RA) narrates, “I remember this saying about the Holy Prophet (PBUH) ‘He (PBUH) was sitting on his camel in Mina. I used to think that 'one goes to the head before making the sacrifice, so I went to the head before the sacrifice.' The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'There is no harm in doing the sacrifice now. There is no harm in it.' I used to think that ``one should clean one's head before throwing pebbles'', so I cleaned one's head before throwing pebbles.'' The same tradition is also narrated along with another document, but in it these words are added: \Departed before hitting the pebbles.\"" This narrator has not been followed in these words and I think the narrator is delusional in quoting these words."""""
"2570","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that I cursed the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of sacrifice, a person attended the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at that time, the Prophet (peace be upon him) was staying near Jamrah. I have shaved my head before throwing pebbles. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Now throw the pebbles, there is no harm.” Then another person came to the service of the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him. He said, “I have sacrificed before throwing the pebbles.” \I have performed Tawaf before throwing pebbles.\"" The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said"","" \""You now throw pebbles. There is no harm.\"" The narrator narrates that on that day"","" I saw you and said that whatever question was asked of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)"","" the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that you should do it now"","" there is no harm."""""
"2571","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that on the Day of Sacrifice, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a person who slaughtered his head with his head before stoning, or sacrificed, or was asked about doing something similar first or later."
"2572","Ata and other narrators have narrated these three things regarding the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: About a person who shaved his head before throwing pebbles. Sacrifice was done. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Now throw pebbles. Sacrifice is part of throwing pebbles and throwing pebbles is like making a sacrifice.” The same hadith has been narrated along with some other isnads, but in them are these words: \Sayyidna Abdullah bin Amr (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) was giving a sermon to us on the day of sacrifice.\"" After that"","" the narrator mentioned the previous hadith"","" which contains these words (the person said)"","" I understood that such and such work precedes such and such (the narrator quoted these words about three works).” So the Prophet"","" may God bless him and grant him peace"","" said"","" “There is nothing wrong with that.”"""""
"2573","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that on the Day of Sacrifice, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was delivering a sermon. A person stood in front of him. He said, \I used to think that such and such work precedes such and such work.\"" Then another person stood up and said"","" O Messenger of God! I used to think that such and such a task is before these three tasks. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said"","" \""Do it now. There is no problem.\"" (The narrator says) On that day"","" the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about anything"","" he said the same thing"","" do it now"","" there is no harm."""""
"2574","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that on the Day of Sacrifice, the Prophet (PBUH) was asked about any work that a person had done before another work, or if one work had been done before another."
"2575","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked, and he (peace be upon him) used to say that there is no problem."
"2576","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that a person came to the service of the Holy Prophet (SAW) and said, “O Messenger of Allah! I have performed Tawaf before playing rummy. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \You now throw pebbles. There is no harm.\"" A person said"","" O Messenger of Allah! I have shaved my head before playing rummy. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said"","" \""There is no problem if you play rummy.\"" One person said"","" \""I have sacrificed before playing rummy.\"""""""
"2577","Imam Jafar Sadiq, may God have mercy on him, quotes this saying of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, regarding his father (Muhammad al-Baqir, may God be pleased with him) with reference to Sayyiduna Jabir, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"2578","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"2579","Imam Jafar Sadiq, may God have mercy on him, narrates this statement of Sayyiduna Jabir, may God bless him and grant him peace, regarding his father (Muhammad al-Baqir, may God be pleased with him). When the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came near Mount Safa, the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited this verse: \Verily"","" Safa and Marwa are the signs of Allah.\"" Allah's Messenger (peace be upon him) started from Safa."""""
"2580","Imam Jafar Sadiq (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates this on the authority of his father (Imam Muhammad Baqir, may Allah have mercy on him) Sayyiduna Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated this. looked at"
"2581","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may God be pleased with him) narrates that when the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Makkah, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) received the black stone and the Yamani stone."
"2582","As soon as Mansoor bin Abdul Rahman quoted this statement of his mother Safiyya, some women belonging to Banu Abdul Dar have said that 'those who were blessed with the time of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him', they told us! Entering the house of Ibn Abi Hussain, we peeped through the door and saw the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) running towards the place of sacrifice until he reached Zakaq Banuflan. This is a place which is called the place of sacrifice. Try because it is obligatory upon you to try."
"2583","Sayyidna Burah bint Abu Tijarrat (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates, “I saw the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ‘When he reached the end of the place of Sa’i, the Prophet (Sallallahu ‘Alaihi Wasallam) said, ‘You people, make Sa’i, because Allah has made it obligatory for you to perform Sa’i (she narrates). Waslam's legs were visible."
"2584","Sayyida Habiba bint Abu Tijarrat (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates, “I saw the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) doing Sa’i between Safa and Marwah."
"2585","A woman named Safiyyah narrates this statement of the daughter of Abu Tujarat: I entered the house of Abu Hussain with some women of the Quraish. I saw the shins. I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: You people, strive because Allah has made it necessary for you to strive."
"2586","A woman belonging to Safiyyah bint Shiba Banu Abddar, who is the daughter of Abu Tjarat, narrates this with reference to her, “She narrates, I entered the house of Aal Abu Hussain with some women of the Quraish, and we saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) (after this, this woman has mentioned according to the previous hadith)."
"2587","Safiyyah Bint Sheebah narrates, I was standing in my window, I saw the Holy Prophet between Safa and Marwah, I saw the Holy Prophet running when he came to the valley."
"2588","Nafee narrates this saying of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, about a bald person, his head will go away."
"2589","Nafee narrates that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) said this about a bald person, his head will be covered with shavings. A narrator named Abdul Kareem has narrated this in my writing, 'Once the narrator has narrated it as a marfu' hadith and once he has not quoted it as a marfu' hadith."
"2590","This same hadith along with another chain of transmission is related to Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"2591","It has been narrated about Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that once he put on Ihram for Umrah, when he reached Dhu al-Halifa, he said, “The case of both of them is one and the same."
"2592","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said: “Whoever wears Ihram for Hajj and Umrah at the same time, it will be sufficient for him to perform Tawaf once and perform Sa’i once, and he will not become halal because of either of them, but he will become halal from both of them."
"2593","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates, “I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying this: Whoever wears Ihram for Hajj and Umrah at the same time, it will be enough for him to perform Tawaf once, then after that he will not open the Haram until he completes his Hajj, then he will open Ihram for both of them at the same time."
"2594","Nafi' narrated this about Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that he once performed Hajj and Umrah together and performed the same effort for both of them and stated that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) also did the same."
"2595","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that once the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed a single Tawaf for the Hajj of the Qur’an, and after doing it, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not open his Ihram."
"2596","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) entered Makkah wearing Ihram for the Hajj of the Qur’an and entered Makkah."
"2597","According to Mujahid Bayan, Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) used to say that when he used to perform Hajj and Umrah at the same time, they both have the same route. This hadith has been narrated only by the narrator named Hasan bin Amara with reference to the narrator named Hakam, and this person is a lost hadeeth."
"2598","Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah, Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar and Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) have narrated that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions circled between Safa and Marwah only once, that was for their Umrah and Hajj."
"2599","This has been narrated about Taus, the narrator narrates, I asked him about Hajj Tamattu, and he said: Sayyiduna Jabar bin Abdullah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated this hadith to me."
"2600","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Tawaf once for both of them and performed Sa’i once for Hajj and Umrah."
"2601","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not perform Tawaf more than once (ie for both Hajj and Umrah)."
"2602","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Hajj and Umrah at the same time."
"2603","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions did not perform Tawaf more than once (i.e. they used to perform Tawaf once for both Hajj and Umrah)."
"2604","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Hajj to the Qur’an, and he performed Tawaf once, both he and his companions. A narrator named Ibn Mubashir has narrated these words, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Tawaf once and performed Sa'i once (the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) also did the same)."
"2605","Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) performed the same Tawaf for Hajj and Umrah."
"2606","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Hajj, but some of his companions did not."
"2607","Sayyidna Zayd bin Arqam, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said that when a person performs Hajj on behalf of his parents, he will be accepted by that person and by his parents, and the souls of both of them (i.e. parents) will be given this good news in heaven, and that person will be recorded as \good\"" in the presence of Allah."""""
"2608","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that whoever performs Hajj on behalf of his parents or performs the duty on their behalf, he will be resurrected on the Day of Resurrection with the righteous people."
"2609","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that a person came to the service of the Holy Prophet (SAW) and said, \My parents have passed away. It was obligatory for them to perform Hajj. Shall I perform Hajj on their behalf?\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said"","" \""What do you think? If your father had a debt"","" would you have paid it on his behalf?\"" He said yes! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said"","" \""You should also perform Hajj on behalf of your father.\"""""""
"2610","Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) said this: Whoever performs Hajj on behalf of his father and mother, then he has fulfilled the obligation of Hajj on their behalf, and this person will receive the reward of performing Hajj ten times."
"2611","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates that a person asked the Prophet (PBUH) that my father had passed away. He had not performed the Hajj. If your father had a debt and you paid it on his behalf, would he accept it? He said yes! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \You should also perform Hajj on his behalf.\"""""""
"2612","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that a person asked the Prophet (PBUH) about performing Hajj on his father's behalf. He said, 'You should perform Hajj on his behalf.' So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is more entitled to this (that his debt be paid)."
"2613","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that when the Holy Prophet (PBUH) performed the Hajj of the Qur’an, it was the occasion of the Farewell Hajj."
"2614","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"2615","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar and Sayyidna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with them) narrate that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Tawaf once for Hajj and Umrah and performed Sa’i only once."
"2616","Imam Jafar Sadiq (RA) narrates this statement of Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) regarding his father (Imam Muhammad Al-Baqir (RA)): The Prophet (PBUH) combined Hajj and Umrah (i.e. performed Hajj of the Qur’an), so he performed Tawaf for both of them once."
"2617","Abdullah Bin Abu Qadah narrates this statement of his father that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions performed Tawaf once for their Hajj and Umrah."
"2618","Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) performed Hajj and Umrah at the same time."
"2619","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) performed Tawaf once for Hajj and Umrah."
"2620","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) performed Tawaf once for Hajj and Umrah, and he did not perform Tawaf again after that."
"2621","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) performed Tawaf once for Hajj and Umrah."
"2622","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may God be pleased with him, explains: No! By Allah! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed tawaf only once for both of them."
"2623","Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said this is enough for you, 'You perform Tawaf once for both of them after Maghrib."
"2624","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"2625","Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said to her that performing Tawaf between As-Safa and Marwah is sufficient for both your Hajj and Umrah."
"2626","According to Mujahid Bayan, Sayyida Ayesha (RA) had menstruation at the place of \Saraf\"" and she was purified from it on the day of 'Arafah"","" then the Prophet (PBUH) said to her"","" \""Performing tawaf between Safa and Marwah will be sufficient for you for both Hajj and Umrah.\"" The words of the tradition are from a narrator named Abu Na'im."""""
"2627","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with him) that the first circumambulation between Safa and Marwah will be sufficient for you for Hajj and Umrah. Narrator Ibn Makhlid has quoted these words: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that your first circumambulation will be sufficient for both your Hajj and Umrah."
"2628","Abd al-Rahman bin Abu Laila narrates that Sayyiduna Ali once performed Hajj and Umrah at the same time, then he performed Tawaf once for both of them, but he performed Sa'i twice for both of them. Hafs bin Abu Dawudnami is a weak narrator while Abdul Rahman bin Abu Laila has a bad memory and his illusions are high."
"2629","Abd al-Rahman bin Abu Laila narrates this about Sayyiduna Ali, he performed Tawaf twice for both Hajj and Umrah, and performed Sa'i twice for both, and said, \I have seen the Holy Prophet"","" may God's prayers and peace be upon him"","" do the same.\"" Hasan bin Amara is an obsolete hadith."""""
"2630","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that when the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Hajj to the Qur’an, he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Tawaf twice and performed Sa’i twice."
"2631","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) performed Tawaf twice for his Umrah and Hajj and performed Sa'i twice. (The narrator narrates) Sayyidna Abu Bakr, Sayyidna Umar, Sayyidna Ali and Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) also did the same. The narrator named Abu Baruh is Amro bin Yazid and this person is also weak."
"2632","Sayyidna Imran bin Hussain (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) performed Tawaf twice and attempted Sa’i twice. Some narrators differ in narrating this hadith. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Hajj and Umrah at the same time. There is no mention of doing Tawaf and Sa'i in this tradition. The narrator named Muhammad bin Yahya has narrated this correct tradition many times and it has also been stated that he had turned away from mentioning Tawaf and Sa'i and started narrating the correct tradition."
"2633","Sayyidna Imran bin Hussain (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) performed Hajj to the Qur'an."
"2634","Abu Muhammad ibn Sa'id narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Zunbur narrated to us; Fudayl ibn 'Iyad narrated to us from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Malik ibn al-Harith—or Mansur, from Malik ibn al-Harith—from Abu Nasr, who said:I met 'Ali when I had entered ihram for Hajj, and he had entered ihram for Hajj and 'Umrah combined. I said: ""Can I do as you did?"" He said: ""That would have been if you had started the 'Umrah first."" I said: ""How do I do it if I want that?"" He said: ""You take a vessel of water and pour it over yourself, then you enter ihram for both together, then you perform two tawafs for them and two sa'ys for them, and your ihram does not become permissible until the Day of Sacrifice.""Mansur said: I mentioned that to Mujahid, and he said: ""We used to give fatwa only for a single tawaf, but as for now, we do not do that."""","" may God be pleased with him"","" 'I had put on Ihram for Hajj"","" while he had put on Ihram for Hajj and Umrah at the same time. I asked if I could do it as you have done.' He said"","" 'It can be done if you perform Umrah first.' He said: Take a pot of water and pour it over you and then put on Ihram for both of them together. Then it will not be permissible for both of them to perform Tawaf twice and perform Sa'i once and for you to open Ihram before the Day of Sacrifice. A narrator named Mansoor narrates that I mentioned this tradition to Mujahid"","" so he said"","" \""We are giving this fatwa. Tawaf will be performed once"","" but now we will not do it.\"""""""
"2635","Imam Shafi'i says this: I adopt people and it is better to have fun. We do not call it makruh."
"2636","Mujahid narrates that Sayyiduna Abu Dharghafari (RA) came, he held the door frame of the Kaaba and then said: I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying that a person should pray after the morning prayer until the sun rises and after the Asr prayer until the sun sets."
"2637","Sayyidna Jubir ibn al-Mu'tam, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates that the Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, said: O Banu Abdul Muttalib! You should not prevent anyone from circumambulating this house and not preventing anyone from offering prayers, whether it is any part of the day or night."
"2638","Sayyidna Jubir ibn al-Mu'tam (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Banu Abd Manaf! This matter is now up to us, so I do not know that you have prevented any person from praying near this house, whether it is any part of the day or night."
"2639","Nafi bin Jubayr quotes the saying of the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, regarding his father, O Banu Abd Manaf! You should not prevent anyone from offering prayers near this house at any part of the day or night."
"2640","Sayyidna Uthman Ghani (RA) quotes the saying of the Holy Prophet (SAW) that a person in the state of Ihram cannot marry himself, he can marry someone. Imam Shafi'i has quoted these words additionally and he cannot even give the message of marriage to anyone."
"2641","Nabiyyah bin Wahhib narrates that Umar bin Ubaidullah sent a message to Aban bin Uthman, 'Iban was the Commander of Hajj in those days, both of them were in the state of Ihram (the message was sent) I want to marry Talha bin Umar with the daughter of Shaiba bin Jubayr, and I want you to be a part of it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has said that a person in the state of Ihram is neither self-respecting, nor can he send a message of marriage to anyone, nor can he marry anyone."
"2642","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a person who was reciting talbiyah by a person named Shabarmah, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called him and said: Have you ever performed Hajj? He did not submit! Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \First"","" perform Hajj on your own behalf"","" then perform Hajj on behalf of Shabarmah.\"""""""
"2643","This tradition is also narrated along with another chain of transmission, but it contains these words: \The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) inquired"","" \""Have you performed Hajj?\"" He did not submit! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then this is from you and later you will perform Hajj from Shabarmah."""""
"2644","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a person reciting talbiya on behalf of another person, so he said to him: O you who recite talbiya on behalf of such and such a person! If you have performed the obligatory Hajj, then recite Talbiyah from Shabarmah, otherwise recite Talbiyah from yourself."
"2645","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed a person who was reciting talbiyah on behalf of a person named Nabisha. This is from Nabeesha, you must first perform Hajj on your own behalf. The narrator named Hasan bin Amara is unique in narrating this hadith and this person is an abandoned hadith."
"2646","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (SAW) passed by a man who was reciting Talbiyah on behalf of Nabisha. It will be from Nabisha, you should perform Hajj from your side."
"2647","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (SAW) heard a person who was reciting Talbiyah on behalf of Nabeesha. Have you done Hajj? He did not submit! The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \Then it will be done by Nabishah. You perform Hajj on your own behalf.\"""""""
"2648","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) cursed a person who was saying, “I am here on behalf of Shabarmah.” The Prophet (PBUH) asked him, “Who is Shabarmah?” He replied, 'My brother.' So he did not submit! The Holy Prophet (PBUH) said, \Perform Hajj on your own behalf"","" then perform Hajj on behalf of Shabarmah.\"" This hadith narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas"","" may Allah be pleased with him"","" is correct. It has been stated that the hadith narrated before it is an illusion. It has been stated that a narrator named Hasan bin Amara narrated it and then turned to him."""""
"2649","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) heard a person saying, “I am here on behalf of Shabarmah.” The Prophet (PBUH) asked, “Have you performed Hajj before?” He did not submit! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \Then it will be done on your behalf. Later"","" you will perform Hajj on behalf of Shabarmah.\"""""""
"2650","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"2651","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) heard a person saying, “I am here on behalf of Shabarmah.” The Prophet (PBUH) said, “Have you performed Hajj on your behalf? He did not submit! He said to the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) then recite Talbiyah on your behalf."
"2652","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"2653","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) passed by a person who was reciting Talbiyah on behalf of another person. If you have not performed the fard, then recite Talbiyah on your own behalf."
"2654","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this on the authority of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): He heard a person reciting Talbiyah on behalf of another person, so he said to him, \If you have performed Hajj on your behalf"","" then recite Talbiyah on his behalf"","" otherwise perform Hajj on your behalf.\"""""""
"2655","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a person saying, “I am here on behalf of Shabarmah.” He did not submit! The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then perform Hajj on your own, then perform Hajj on behalf of Shabarmah."
"2656","Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) heard a person reciting talbiyah by Shabarma, so he inquired who is Shabarma? This person mentioned his relationship with him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Have you performed Hajj yourself? Narrator states that this person answered no! Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, then first you perform Hajj on your behalf, then you perform Hajj on behalf of Shubarmah."
"2657","Another chain of transmission is similar to the (past hadith) of Ibn Abi Laila."
"2658","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a person saying, “I am here on behalf of Shabarmah.” The Prophet (peace be upon him) asked who is Shabarmah? He replied that he is my brother (the narrator doubts that maybe these are the words) He mentioned his relationship. So he said no. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \Then do it on your behalf and later perform Hajj on behalf of Shubarmah.\"""""""
"2659","The same tradition is also narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, it contains these words: \You should do it on your own side"","" then perform Hajj on behalf of Shabarmah.\"""""""
"2660","This tradition is narrated as a marfu' hadith along with another chain of transmission."
"2661","Along with another chain of transmission, it is narrated that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a person saying, “I am here on behalf of Shabarmah” (following this is according to the previous hadith)."
"2662","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) heard a person reciting talbiyah by Shabarmah and inquired who is Shabarmah? He replied that he is my brother, or I am related to him. He did not submit! The Holy Prophet (peace be upon him) said, \Do it on your behalf\"" then he would perform Hajj on his behalf."""""
"2663","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) heard a person saying Talbiyah by Shabarmah and asked him, \Have you performed Hajj?\"" He submitted! The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said"","" \""Then recite the talbiyah on your own behalf.\"""""""
"2664","Saeed bin Jubayr narrates this about Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, he saw a person reciting talbiya from Shabarmah."
"2665","This tradition has been narrated as a muquf tradition from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may God be pleased with him) along with another chain of transmission."
"2666","Safiyyah Bint Sheeba narrates Umm Uthman Bint Abu Sufyan has narrated this, Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Abbas (RA) has narrated this. The Prophet (PBUH) said, “It is not obligatory on women to shave their heads. Women will only cut their hair short."
"2667","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that shaving the head is not for women."
"2668","Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Umar Radiyallahu Anhu says this about a woman in the state of Ihram, she will cut as much hair as her index finger."
"2669","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) says this: The sunnah is that on the night of putting on Ihram, a woman will put some henna on her head, then wash her head and put it on her head."
"2670","Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) gave permission to women to wear socks in the state of Ihram. Salim narrates that earlier Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) used to call it makruh, until a woman named Safiyyah narrated this hadith regarding Sayyida Aisha (RA) (so he issued a fatwa according to it)."
"2671","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) used to give this fatwa that women should cut off their socks, until Safiyyah told him that Sayyida Aisha (RA) had instructed women not to cut them off. This tradition is suspended."
"2672","Ata narrates that once a man had intercourse with his wife before circumambulating Baitullah on the Day of Sacrifice, then Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) said that they will both sacrifice a camel, but now it will not be obligatory for them to perform Hajj again next year."
"2673","Ibrahim bin Abdullah narrates this statement of his father. Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas and Sayyidna Masurab bin Mukharama had a disagreement about whether a person in the state of Ihram can shed his head or not. So these gentlemen sent me to the service of Ayyub Ansari (RA) so that I could find out from whom they had seen the Prophet (PBUH) 'The Prophet (PBUH) used to wash himself in his state of Ihram (or not)', then Sayyidna Ayub Ansari (RA) poured water on his head, 'moved his hand to the front and brought it back from the back."
"2674","Sayyidna Mu'awiya bin Khadij (RA) narrates that he was present at the service of the Holy Prophet (PBUH) and his mother Kabsha bint Maadi Karb was present with him. Her mother said, O Messenger of Allah! I have made this vow, 'I will circumambulate the house of Sirin', so the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, 'Walk on your feet and perform circumambulation' seven times with both hands and seven times with both feet."
"2675","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) has narrated the saying of the Holy Prophet (PBUH): Do not throw pebbles at Jamrat until the sun rises."
"2676","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed his wives to leave Muzdalifah at night and throw pebbles at Jamrat, then return to their place of residence in the morning, so those women continued to do so until they died (i.e. they continued to do so for the rest of their lives). Ata states that we will continue to do the same."
"2677","Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (RA) narrates that when the Prophet (PBUH) completed his Hajj, I perfumed the Prophet (PBUH) before performing his circumambulation."
"2678","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that I perfumed the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with my two hands when he shaved his head after slaughtering an animal."
"2679","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that I perfumed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) before he put on his Ihram and before performing Tawaf when he took off his Ihram (perfumed him)."
"2680","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that on the last day of sacrifice, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came back. He offered the Zuhr prayer, then he went back and spent the nights of Tashreek in the moon. He also stopped and stood there for a long time praying (with Griya Waziri) then did not stop there at the time of pelting pebbles on the third Jamrah."
"2681","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) went on foot to throw stones and returned on foot. During this time, he did not ride a horse. Sayyidna Abu Bakr and Sayyidna Umar also used to do the same."
"2682","Sayyidna Jabar bin Abdullah (RA) narrates, “I remember this saying about the Holy Prophet (SAW) ‘He (SAW) threw pebbles at Jamrah on the Day of Sacrifice at Chasht, and then after that he (SAW) threw pebbles at it at the time of sunset. Ibn Abu Shaybah narrates that stones will be thrown at the time of chasht on the day of sacrifice at Jamrah al-Uqbah, and the next day when the sun sets."
"2683","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"2684","Zahri narrates that when the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) threw pebbles at the Jamra which is near the Mina Mosque, he hit it with seven pebbles. While throwing each pebble, he said Takbeer. Then he came in front of the Jamra and stood facing the House of Allah. Throwing each pebble, he said Takbeer, then he moved a little to the left, which is Wadi Wal-Hisa, then he stood there facing the House of Allah, he raised both his hands and began to pray. Come, then you did not stand next to him. Al-Zuhri has narrated this. The narrator narrates that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar used to do the same thing."
"2685","Amro bin Shuaib narrates from his father, \The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave permission to herdsmen to throw pebbles at night\"" or at any time during the day."""""
"2686","Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa Radiyallahu Anha narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, when a man throws pebbles, shaves his head, and speaks with his mouth, then he becomes lawful for everything, but he cannot have intercourse with his wife."
"2687","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: When you throw pebbles and make sacrifices, you will become lawful for everything (but you cannot have intercourse with women)."
"2688","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that when you throw pebbles, make sacrifices, you become lawful for everything, but you cannot have intercourse with a woman. This same hadith along with another chain of transmission has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa."
"2689","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that on the night of sacrifice, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a message to Umm Salama."
"2690","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that when a person starts going back, he should circumambulate the Bayt Allah last, but this is not an order for menstruating women, because the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has given them this permission (they can go back without circumambulating the House of Allah for the last time). A narrator named Abu Ammar has stated that a person who performs Hajj to Bait Allah should perform Tawaf of Bait Allah at the end, however, the order for menstruating women is different, because the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has given them permission (that they may go back without performing Tawaf)."
"2691","Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'id and Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Mubashshir narrated to us; they said: Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam Abu al-Ash'ath narrated to us; Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us; from Ayyub; from Ibrahim ibn Maysarah; from Tawus, who said: I was sitting with Abdullah ibn Umar when he was asked about that — meaning the menstruating woman departing (before the farewell circumambulation). He said: ""She must remain until her last act is at the House (the Ka'bah)."" Tawus said: So I do not know whether Ibn Umar forgot it or had not heard what his companions heard. Then, after a year or two, I witnessed him being asked about it, and he said: ""I have been informed that a concession was granted to them."""","" may Allah be pleased with him. He was asked about this"","" that is"","" about the return of a menstruating woman. He said"","" 'She will stay there until she performs Tawaf of the House of Allah for the last time.' Yadusal was present with him later"","" and he was asked about it"","" and he said"","" \""It has been explained to me that these women are allowed to do so (they can go back without performing Tawaf)."""""
"2692","Sayyiduna Hajjaj bin Amr Ansari (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that a person who becomes injured or disabled will take off his ihram and it will be obligatory for him to perform Hajj the following year."
"2693","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) has said that whoever performs Hajj and comes to visit my grave after I leave, it is said that he came to visit me during my lifetime."
"2694","Sayyiduna Hatib narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that whoever came to visit me after my death, it is said that he came to visit me during my lifetime, and whoever dies in one of Makkah or Madinah will be resurrected with the believers on the Day of Resurrection."
"2695","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (SAW) said that whoever visits my grave, my intercession will be obligatory for him."
"2696","Imam Jafar Sadiq, may God have mercy on him, narrates this statement of Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah regarding his father (Imam Muhammad Baqir, may God have mercy on him)."
"2697","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may God be pleased with him, narrates that Iqra bin Habs asked the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, whether it is obligatory to perform Hajj every year. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No, it is obligatory to perform Hajj once, and whoever performs Hajj after that, it will be Nafil for him."
"2698","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said, “O people! If Hajj was made obligatory on you, then Iqra bin Habs (RA) said, O Messenger of Allah, is it obligatory to perform Hajj every year? The Prophet (PBUH) remained silent, then he said, No, but it is obligatory to perform Hajj only once. After that, whoever performs Hajj will have Nafl for him."
"2699","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that Iqra bin Habs (may Allah be pleased with him) asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the Hajj every year."
"2700","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"2701","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"2702","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that when the Holy Prophet (PBUH) ordered to perform Hajj, Iqra Bin Habis (RA) asked: Is it obligatory to perform Hajj every year? Ya Rasulullah! The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If I had said yes, then it would have become obligatory."
"2703","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates when this verse was revealed. \And it is obligatory upon the people to perform Hajj to the House of Allah for the sake of Allah"","" whoever has the means to reach it.\"" People asked"","" O Messenger of Allah"","" is it obligatory to perform Hajj every year? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained silent. The people said: Is it obligatory every year? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No"","" if I had said yes"","" it would have become necessary. Then Allah revealed this verse. \""O believers! Do not discover things which"","" if revealed to you"","" would make you feel bad. There are these words in a tradition"","" people asked what every year? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained silent"","" then the people asked"","" \""What about every year?\"" Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said:"""""
"2704","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that a person asked the Prophet (PBUH) in a loud voice whether it is obligatory to perform Hajj every year. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained silent, then he said no! On the contrary, it is obligatory for a Muslim to perform Hajj once every year. If I had said it every year, it would have become obligatory every year. Another person stood up and asked, \Can I perform Hajj on behalf of my father because he is an elderly man?\"""""""
"2705","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) was giving a sermon and the Prophet (PBUH) said, “O people! Allah has made Hajj obligatory upon you. Then a man stood up and said, O Messenger of Allah, is it obligatory to perform Hajj every year? He asked this question three times. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not give him any answer. When I command you to do something, do it as much as you can, and when I forbid you to do something, refrain from it."
"2706","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: Once the Prophet (PBUH) stood among us to deliver a sermon and said: O people! Allah Ta'ala has made it obligatory upon you to perform Hajj."
"2707","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Allah's Messenger (may peace be upon him) said this: O people, performing Hajj has been made obligatory upon you. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not give him any answer, he repeated the question, he asked, O Messenger of Allah, what every year? The Holy Prophet (peace be upon him) said: Who is the one who said this? The people said that there is such and such a person. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, \By the One in Whose Power is my life. If I had said yes"","" it would have become obligatory. If it had become obligatory"","" you would not have been able to pay it"","" and if you were not able to do it"","" then you would have committed disbelief. So Allah revealed this verse. \""O believers! Do not inquire about such things which"","" if they were revealed to you"","" would lead you astray."""""
"2708","Yahya bin Ya'Umar narrates: I said to Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, some people say that there is no reality of fate. So Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said, \If you meet him"","" convey this message to me that Abdullah bin Umar requests in the presence of Allah to be indifferent to you and you have nothing to do with him.\"" (Then Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrated this hadith. I heard Sayyidna Umar Bin Khattab narrating that he said that one day we were sitting with the Prophet (PBUH) in the presence of some people"","" while a man came there"","" he had no sign of travel and he was not a resident of the city. He placed his hand on the knees of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said"","" O Sayyidna Muhammad"","" what is Islam? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said"","" “Islam is that you bear witness that there is no god but Allah"","" and that Muhammad (peace be upon him) is the Messenger of Allah"","" and establish prayer"","" and pay Zakat"","" and perform Hajj"","" and perform Umrah"","" and perform ablution"","" and perform ablution"","" and observe the fast of Ramadan. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said yes. After that"","" he narrated the rest of the hadith. At the end of this hadith"","" the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said"","" \""Block this person to me.\"" (says the narrator) We went out in search of him"","" but we could not find him. Sometimes I had a hard time recognizing them and I recognized them when they left. The chain of transmission of this hadith is proven and correct"","" Imam Muslim has narrated it with the same chain of transmission."""""
"2709","Sayyiduna Saraqa bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates, I asked, O Messenger of Allah, is the order of Umrah specific to us this year or is it for forever? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “No, it is forever, Umrah has entered Hajj until the Day of Judgment (meaning both of them can be performed together). All the narrators of this tradition are authentic."
"2710","Sayyidna Aburzain (RA) narrates that he asked the Prophet (PBUH) this question. He said, \My father has become old. He has become a Muslim"","" but now he cannot perform Umrah and travel. The Prophet (PBUH) said"","" 'You should perform both Hajj and Umrah on behalf of your father.'"""""
"2711","Sayyida Umm Salma narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that whoever wears the Ihram of Hajj and Umrah to go from Masjid Al-Aqsa to Masjid Haram, all past and future sins of that person will be forgiven, and Paradise will be obligatory for him."
"2712","Sayyidah Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “Whoever puts on the Ihram for Hajj or Umrah from Bait al-Maqdis, he will become from his sins as he was on the day his mother gave birth to him."
"2713","Sayyida Umm Salma (RA) narrates that the Holy Prophet (PBUH) said that whoever wears Ihram for Hajj or Umrah from Bait-ul-Maqdis, his past sins will be forgiven."
"2714","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (SAW) that whoever performs Hajj or Umrah and does not commit any filth or immorality during it, when he returns, he will be as he was on the day his mother gave birth to him."
"2715","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that she asked the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) whether it is necessary to wage Jihad on women."
"2716","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates, I asked, O Messenger of Allah, is it obligatory for women to wage Jihad?"
"2717","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates that Hajj and Umrah are compulsory for all people, only the people of Makkah have a different ruling, since their Umrah must be circumambulated. When the Holy Prophet (peace be upon him) entered Makkah, he was wearing Ihram for Hajj or Ihram for Umrah."
"2718","Sayyidna Zaid bin Thabit (RA) narrates that the Prophet (PBUH) said that Hajj and Umrah are both obligatory."
"2719","It is narrated that Sayyiduna Zayd bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) was asked about performing Umrah before Hajj, and he said that these are two prayers."
"2720","Narrated by Nafi, Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) used to say that Hajj and Umrah are obligatory on all of God's creation, that is, on those who have the means to go there, and if a person does more after that, then it is good and a posthumous act of worship. The narrator narrates, I heard him say something about the people of Makkah."
"2721","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that performing Umrah is obligatory like Hajj and it is a short Hajj."
